    "chapter": "Decision Making and Risk",
    "topic": "Uncertainty- Decision Making",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Sometimes decisions are made in the face of total ambiguity: On how likely any state of nature is, there is no information. </p>\r\n<p>When a decision is made, the person making it has no control over and is unsure of which future natural conditions will take place. </p>\r\n<p>Let's say a distribution business is thinking about getting a computer to help them handle more orders. The company will see a significant gain in profit if the economy stays strong; however, if the economy suffers, the company will experience a loss. </p>\r\n<p>The two choices available are to buy the computer and not to buy the computer.</p>",
