    "discipline": "Industrial",
    "subject": "Manufacturing, Service, and Other Production Systems",
    "chapter": "Planning and Scheduling",
    "topic": "Sequencing",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "Priority Sequencing Rules \r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Priority Rules provide guidelines for the sequence in which jobs should be worked. </li>\r\n<li>In using this rules, job processing times and due dates are important pieces of information.</li>\r\n<li>Priority Rules try to minimize completion time, number of jobs in the system, and job lateness, while maximizing facility utilization.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nPriority Sequencing Rules\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>First come, first served (FCFS) </li>\r\n<li>Shortest processing time (SPT)</li> \r\n<li>Earlier due date (EDD) </li>\r\n<li>Critical Ratio (CR)</li>\r\n</ol>",
