    "discipline": "Industrial",
    "subject": "Manufacturing, Service, and Other Production Systems",
    "chapter": "Process Improvements",
    "topic": "Lean Systems",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>An ideology of maximizing productivity </li>\r\n<li>Simultaneously minimizing waste within a manufacturing operation </li>\r\n<li>Reduced lead times, operating costs and improved product quality.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nAdvantages of Lean Systems:\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Saves Time and Money </li>\r\n<li>Environment friendly </li>\r\n<li>Improve customer satisfaction </li>\r\n<li>Divide work load </li>\r\n<li>Reduce rework, waste </li>\r\n<li>Improve quality</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7d/ISO_18404_Focus_of_Lean_and_Six_Sigma.png\" alt=\"Focus of Lean and Six Sigma\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISO_18404_Focus_of_Lean_and_Six_Sigma.png\">PRWhitehouse</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
