    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n\r\n<p>Time study provides standard time, which is the amount of time it takes workers to complete a job in a standard way. A good estimate requires standard times for various jobs.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Labor, machinery and equipment requirements</li>\r\n<li>Daily, weekly or monthly material requirements</li>\r\n<li>Cost of production per unit as an input to improve manufacturing or purchasing decisions</li>\r\n<li>Work budget</li>\r\n<li>Worker Efficiency and Incentive Payments.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Time_study_stopwatch.JPG\" alt=\"Time study stopwatch\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Time_study_stopwatch.JPG\">Tasma3197</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
